WEBVTT

1
00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.095
Stop, kid!

2
00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.308
Stop right there!

3
00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.394
It's just a stupid car.

4
00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.437
You're gonna make it worse on yourself.

5
00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.026
Freeze! Stop! Freeze!

6
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.320
Stop right there!

7
00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:47.458
Now, bud, come on.
We're going over to the wall.

8
00:02:48.626 --> 00:02:50.670
Get this hand behind your back!
There you go.

9
00:02:50.753 --> 00:02:53.840
- What are the odds we call this a warning?
- Not good.

10
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:56.509
Let's go! We're going!

11
00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:05.809
Will.

12
00:03:10.481 --> 00:03:12.275
You stole a cop car.

13
00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.363
Six years. Seven schools.

14
00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:19.574
Twenty-two homes.

15
00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:22.660
That's gotta be a record,
and not one to be proud of.

16
00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:25.121
It's hard not to see it
as an accomplishment.

17
00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.998
I'm glad you think it's funny.

18
00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.709
This time it's serious, Will.

19
00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:33.379
That leaves me no choice
but to remand you to a state facility.

20
00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:37.007
Juvie?

21
00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:40.470
Mark, come on, you can't be serious.

22
00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:43.556
- You've been through a lot.
- I'll do better.

23
00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.766
You're smart.

24
00:03:45.975 --> 00:03:48.061
- Talented.
- Hey, I'll change.

25
00:03:48.144 --> 00:03:49.354
For real this time.

26
00:03:49.437 --> 00:03:52.065
- There's gotta be something else!
- There's not.

27
00:03:54.692 --> 00:03:58.071
I'm sorry, Will.
That group home was the last option.

28
00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:05.703
I know it's been hard since you lost
your parents, but you're a great kid.

29
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.040
I just hope for your own sake,

30
00:04:09.123 --> 00:04:12.043
you figure that out
sooner rather than later.

31
00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:17.840
Hey Mark,
Kristin's here to see you.

32
00:04:27.225 --> 00:04:28.225
Wait here.

33
00:04:28.851 --> 00:04:29.978
I'll be right back.

34
00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.608
- Hey, Kristin, how are you?
- I'm fine. Thanks.

35
00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:36.692
Kristin.

36
00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:05.013
One, two, three, make a wish!

37
00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.769
Well, today's your lucky day.

38
00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:14.439
Good news. This is Kristin.

39
00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:18.026
She's one of our foster parents
and her son.

40
00:05:18.109 --> 00:05:19.694
George. I'm George.

41
00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:22.363
Umm...

42
00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:24.365
- Hi.
- Nice to meet ya.

43
00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:28.745
- You too.
- Will, I was discussing it with Mark,

44
00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.539
and we would be excited
if you would join us this year.

45
00:05:32.415 --> 00:05:33.458
Where?

46
00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:38.004
You are going to summer camp.

47
00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:41.049
Mark, I'm not really camp material.

48
00:05:44.969 --> 00:05:48.222
All right then, uh, juvie it is.

49
00:05:48.306 --> 00:05:50.600
- Sorry, guys, thanks for trying.
- Wait, juvie?

50
00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.685
George, he doesn't want to go.

51
00:05:57.565 --> 00:05:58.733
No, hey, wait.

52
00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:07.533
- Summer camp sounds perfect.
- You're gonna love it.

53
00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:11.788
You are gonna love it.

54
00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:16.709
I'm so totally excited. You play guitar.
We're gonna rock the talent show.

55
00:06:16.793 --> 00:06:19.420
Plus, there's swimming
in the lake, a zip line.

56
00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:21.631
It's gonna be epic.
I'll show you the ropes.

57
00:06:43.694 --> 00:06:44.821
Let's go.

58
00:06:49.951 --> 00:06:51.536
- And you.
- Me?

59
00:07:46.757 --> 00:07:47.757
This is weird.

60
00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:49.677
It's gonna be great!

61
00:07:54.557 --> 00:07:55.641
- Nope.
- Come on.

62
00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:48.693
Hi.

63
00:08:49.445 --> 00:08:50.445
Hi.

64
00:08:51.239 --> 00:08:52.239
I'm...

65
00:08:52.573 --> 00:08:54.534
Um, Avery.

66
00:08:54.617 --> 00:08:56.619
Nice to meet you, um, Avery.

67
00:09:03.084 --> 00:09:04.627
We're gonna kill it, baby.

68
00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.212
- I'm sure you will.
- Will!

69
00:09:06.796 --> 00:09:10.967
- Oh, Will, there you are.
- So, I'm guessing it's Will?

70
00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:17.640
Yeah, Avery, Sean,
and Sean's squad. This is Will.

71
00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:20.643
New kid. Nice to meet you.

72
00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:21.852
You too.

73
00:09:21.936 --> 00:09:26.732
- So, how do you two know each other?
- Um, Will is my...

74
00:09:26.816 --> 00:09:30.236
We're family, cousins.
I'm visiting from Philly for the summer.

75
00:09:30.319 --> 00:09:31.319
Yes.

76
00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.240
- Family.
- Mm-hmm.

77
00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:36.659
What about you? Where are you from?

78
00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:40.538
I just got back from the Arctic,
helping to save the narwhals.

79
00:09:40.621 --> 00:09:42.081
- Narwhals?
- Yes.

80
00:09:42.164 --> 00:09:45.710
I didn't think those were real.
I thought they were like unicorns.

81
00:09:45.793 --> 00:09:47.253
Majestic unicorns of the sea.

82
00:09:49.547 --> 00:09:52.508
I'm just doing my part, you know?

83
00:09:53.301 --> 00:09:55.136
- Taking this one next year.
- What?

84
00:09:55.219 --> 00:09:56.053
- Right?
- What?

85
00:09:56.137 --> 00:09:57.054
- Taking her?
- Yeah.

86
00:09:57.138 --> 00:10:00.224
- I actually never said that.
- All right, fellas.

87
00:10:43.684 --> 00:10:45.561
Yes sir.

88
00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:48.105
That's what I do.

89
00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:50.691
Wow. Is he for real?

90
00:10:51.692 --> 00:10:54.737
He is very, very real. Anyway...

91
00:11:25.893 --> 00:11:27.728
Hi, George.

92
00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:30.272
Come on.

93
00:11:30.356 --> 00:11:32.566
You didn't tell me
this was church camp.

94
00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:38.280
- Hey, David.
- Hey!

95
00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:40.825
It's the last week of summer.
Are you ready?

96
00:11:40.908 --> 00:11:44.578
Five hundred percent.
Leaves and hearts will be a-changing.

97
00:11:44.662 --> 00:11:47.498
Yes! So what do you
have planned for the tribunal?

98
00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:49.458
It's pretty exciting. Two words.

99
00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:51.252
Braveheart!

100
00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.130
Well, that's actually one word.

101
00:11:55.756 --> 00:12:00.010
Oh! Look, here's Will Hawkins' file.

102
00:12:00.094 --> 00:12:02.930
- Oh, right.
- Social Services put everything in there.

103
00:12:03.556 --> 00:12:06.434
What's this? Is this real?

104
00:12:06.517 --> 00:12:08.769
He tried to sell his high school
on Craigslist?

105
00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:12.106
- Mm-hmm! That boy got three offers.
- Okay.

106
00:12:12.189 --> 00:12:14.984
Uh, is this kid something
I gotta be worried about?

107
00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:18.195
I seem to remember
a certain bad boy back in the day.

108
00:12:18.863 --> 00:12:21.532
Yeah, back when I had
a glorious head of man-hair.

109
00:12:21.615 --> 00:12:25.494
Relax, Fabio. Will will be fine.

110
00:12:25.578 --> 00:12:28.456
George is showing him the ropes.
It's actually kinda cute.

111
00:12:28.539 --> 00:12:32.293
- You got him staying in the...
- Yeah, the legit cabin.

112
00:12:32.376 --> 00:12:34.086
- Yeah, it's, um...
- It's...

113
00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:35.838
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

114
00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:37.590
- It is.
- It is.

115
00:12:44.388 --> 00:12:46.265
Mmm. She's a classic.

116
00:12:48.225 --> 00:12:49.477
That's a word for it.

117
00:12:51.145 --> 00:12:52.646
Hello, old friend.

118
00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.274
You actually chose this cabin?

119
00:12:55.357 --> 00:12:57.526
Yeah, I mean, who wouldn't?

120
00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:02.865
The toilet backs up, when it works.
There's no AC... Oh, and the spiders.

121
00:13:02.948 --> 00:13:04.158
Spiders?

122
00:13:05.701 --> 00:13:07.953
I guess they haven't
come out yet. Anyway.

123
00:13:08.037 --> 00:13:09.037
Oh well.

124
00:13:09.705 --> 00:13:14.668
Oh, by the way, what was that back there?
The whole family slash cousins thing?

125
00:13:14.752 --> 00:13:17.213
I don't mean to be a prude,

126
00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:21.175
but lying's up there on the top ten
"Thou shalt nots."

127
00:13:21.258 --> 00:13:24.386
I wasn't ready.
It made me kinda uncomfortable.

128
00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.931
- It doesn't really fly...
- Yeah, I totally get it.

129
00:13:27.848 --> 00:13:29.809
- Oh, you get it?
- Yeah, I do.

130
00:13:29.892 --> 00:13:31.477
Great.

131
00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:34.063
That's a relief 'cause
I'm not trying to be uncool.

132
00:13:34.146 --> 00:13:35.146
You like the view.

133
00:13:35.689 --> 00:13:36.689
What?

134
00:13:36.732 --> 00:13:37.732
The view.

135
00:13:40.986 --> 00:13:44.198
- No, that's not it at all.
- Careful. Lies are up there.

136
00:13:45.366 --> 00:13:46.408
What's her name?

137
00:13:49.787 --> 00:13:51.747
Presley Elizabeth Borsky.

138
00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.458
Dean's list four years straight.

139
00:13:54.542 --> 00:13:58.712
Loves all things cute and cuddly,
specifically anything pug-related.

140
00:13:59.463 --> 00:14:01.924
She wears the perfect
little shoe size.

141
00:14:03.509 --> 00:14:05.094
Seven and a half, narrow.

142
00:14:07.304 --> 00:14:10.891
We're gonna have to work on
this stalker vibe you got going on.

143
00:14:12.476 --> 00:14:14.687
What about Avery? What's her story?

144
00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:17.439
Way out of your league.
Trust me.

145
00:14:18.107 --> 00:14:19.483
Really? Ouch.

146
00:14:19.567 --> 00:14:21.068
Yeah, how should I say this?

147
00:14:21.151 --> 00:14:25.739
I don't know if she'd be into the whole
"stealing a cop car" kinda guy.

148
00:14:26.782 --> 00:14:31.203
First of all, borrowed a cop car.
Second of all, how did you even know that?

149
00:14:31.287 --> 00:14:33.831
Oh. Georgie's got ears everywhere.

150
00:14:34.415 --> 00:14:36.750
Well, then,
what would she be into?

151
00:14:36.834 --> 00:14:38.127
Like, what's her deal?

152
00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:41.589
Uh, this camp, honestly.

153
00:14:41.672 --> 00:14:44.258
She practically lives here.
Her dad owns the place.

154
00:14:44.341 --> 00:14:45.426
What about her mom?

155
00:14:46.302 --> 00:14:49.430
Let me guess, she's off
saving the world like Mother Teresa.

156
00:14:49.513 --> 00:14:50.806
No. She's...

157
00:14:52.266 --> 00:14:53.976
Doesn't really talk about it.

158
00:14:55.269 --> 00:14:58.188
She spends most of the summer
as a counselor and, uh,

159
00:14:58.272 --> 00:15:01.775
this is the only time
she gets to be a normal camper like us.

160
00:15:01.859 --> 00:15:04.695
And watch out, she's crazy competitive.

161
00:15:04.778 --> 00:15:07.239
That makes two of us.

162
00:15:08.866 --> 00:15:11.702
George, you said that telling
the truth wasn't an option.

163
00:15:11.785 --> 00:15:17.333
No. I'm just not super sure
Avery would be into it.

164
00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:19.919
That kinda sounds
like the same thing, dude.

165
00:15:21.211 --> 00:15:23.714
I have to make this camp thing work. Okay?

166
00:15:24.298 --> 00:15:27.134
If I'm going to fit here,
I have to be something I'm not.

167
00:15:27.217 --> 00:15:28.260
That's where you come in.

168
00:15:28.344 --> 00:15:29.345
- Right, Georgie?
- Um...

169
00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:33.140
How about this? If you help me,
then I'll help you

170
00:15:33.223 --> 00:15:37.019
with Miss Presley Elizabeth Borscht.

171
00:15:37.686 --> 00:15:39.396
- Borscht? Barber?
- Borsky.

172
00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.689
Borksy! Right.

173
00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:43.901
All you gotta do is keep our secret,
show me the ropes.

174
00:15:44.401 --> 00:15:45.401
That's it.

175
00:15:45.903 --> 00:15:47.279
So I guess I'd be like...

176
00:15:48.364 --> 00:15:50.282
Your Yoda, I will be.

177
00:15:50.366 --> 00:15:53.035
- Yes. Sure. My Yoda.
- Mmm.

178
00:15:53.118 --> 00:15:56.664
- Lesson one, my young Padawan.
- You can stop talking like that.

179
00:15:56.747 --> 00:15:58.958
Shorts, wear them, you must.

180
00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:06.799
You're welcome.
Got plenty. Welcome to camp.

181
00:16:07.591 --> 00:16:09.301
You're a really weird dude.

182
00:16:12.388 --> 00:16:13.388
Thank you.

183
00:16:16.642 --> 00:16:18.102
Why are they so itchy?

184
00:16:18.185 --> 00:16:21.981
Polyester blend. Or as I like to call it,
God's gift to fashion.

185
00:16:22.064 --> 00:16:23.524
I smell like old people.

186
00:16:23.607 --> 00:16:26.944
This is my super real cousin Will,
just visiting from out of town.

187
00:16:27.027 --> 00:16:28.696
- We're related.
- Easy, tiger.

188
00:16:29.488 --> 00:16:32.199
- What's the plan, Rain Man?
- Take your pick.

189
00:16:32.282 --> 00:16:34.868
- Archery, baking club...
- Oh, what about that?

190
00:16:34.952 --> 00:16:36.704
Nope. Don't do heights.

191
00:16:37.413 --> 00:16:39.748
Okay, we are definitely
signing up for that.

192
00:16:39.832 --> 00:16:44.086
Uh, no paintball, I never do paintball,
I wasn't really built for that.

193
00:16:44.169 --> 00:16:46.672
- Today's the day.
- No, stop, don't go over there.

194
00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:50.009
- I don't want to. Don't invalidate me.
- Hey, guys, how's it going?

195
00:16:50.092 --> 00:16:53.804
Hey! It's, um, it's Will, right?

196
00:16:53.887 --> 00:16:57.099
- Ah! Good memory, um, Avery.
- Thanks. Funny.

197
00:16:57.182 --> 00:17:00.728
- Let me guess, you're on the red team?
- Yeah, Crimson Angels.

198
00:17:00.811 --> 00:17:02.604
Did you come up with that name?

199
00:17:03.272 --> 00:17:04.106
Why?

200
00:17:04.189 --> 00:17:07.484
I'm just trying to decide
how honest to be in my opinion.

201
00:17:07.568 --> 00:17:09.361
Oh! That's funny.

202
00:17:09.445 --> 00:17:13.240
I, uh, was thinking the same thing
about your shorts.

203
00:17:13.323 --> 00:17:15.909
Touché.

204
00:17:15.993 --> 00:17:17.578
And you must be Presley.

205
00:17:17.661 --> 00:17:20.748
- Yeah, hi, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

206
00:17:21.331 --> 00:17:22.541
Hey, George.

207
00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:28.630
George was actually just telling me
all about you earlier.

208
00:17:28.714 --> 00:17:29.965
- Really?
- No, no, no...

209
00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:31.800
- Nothing weird or anything.
- Right.

210
00:17:31.884 --> 00:17:34.553
- I... We're cousins for the summer.
- I love the summer.

211
00:17:34.636 --> 00:17:37.306
- He's my cousin and we're here.
- Cool.

212
00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:38.557
- The summer.
- It's okay.

213
00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.185
I was just showing him around. No biggie.

214
00:17:41.268 --> 00:17:43.562
That's awesome, George.

215
00:17:43.645 --> 00:17:44.855
Y-yeah.

216
00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.300
This'll be fun to do it together.

217
00:17:49.359 --> 00:17:50.611
- Where do I sign?
- Here.

218
00:17:50.694 --> 00:17:53.363
- Don't write my name. Forgery.
- I'm signing your name.

219
00:17:53.447 --> 00:17:55.616
- You'll be great.
- Excited, because...

220
00:17:55.699 --> 00:17:57.576
There we go.

221
00:17:57.659 --> 00:17:59.244
Thanks.

222
00:18:00.079 --> 00:18:01.246
Good luck, Will...

223
00:18:02.122 --> 00:18:03.122
Hawkins.

224
00:18:04.124 --> 00:18:05.209
You're gonna need it.

225
00:18:05.292 --> 00:18:06.502
- Luck?
- Yeah.

226
00:18:07.544 --> 00:18:08.879
- Okay.
- Okay.

227
00:18:08.962 --> 00:18:11.048
- See you there.
- See you around, George.

228
00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:15.844
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

229
00:18:16.929 --> 00:18:19.098
That was good. You looked good.
That time.

230
00:18:19.181 --> 00:18:22.643
- Dude, what was that?
- I know.

231
00:18:22.726 --> 00:18:25.395
I can talk to anybody
but Presley. It sucks.

232
00:18:25.479 --> 00:18:28.065
So, it looks like George
still has a thing for you.

233
00:18:28.148 --> 00:18:29.983
Come on, he can't even look at me.

234
00:18:30.067 --> 00:18:34.613
Presley could have any guy she wants.
Trust me, all right? I tried last year.

235
00:18:34.696 --> 00:18:36.949
I wrote her a letter every single day.

236
00:18:38.534 --> 00:18:39.743
I didn't ever send them.

237
00:18:39.827 --> 00:18:41.829
Maybe you should invest in some stamps.

238
00:18:41.912 --> 00:18:44.790
I'm telling you,
if the two of you just would talk.

239
00:18:44.873 --> 00:18:46.250
You just gotta talk to her.

240
00:18:47.584 --> 00:18:48.584
Yeah.

241
00:18:50.504 --> 00:18:51.504
Dude, come on.

242
00:20:03.744 --> 00:20:05.162
- Eh. That's true.
- Come on.

243
00:20:36.151 --> 00:20:37.151
Okay.

244
00:21:36.378 --> 00:21:38.213
- Lay of the land.
- Hit me.

245
00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:40.382
Camp's divided into three teams.
I'm Verdes Maximus.

246
00:21:40.465 --> 00:21:42.718
- Georgie boy and new kid!
- Looking good, Stuart.

247
00:21:42.801 --> 00:21:45.637
- Excuse me? Did you call me Stuart?
- He's turning around.

248
00:21:45.721 --> 00:21:47.681
Oh my gosh.
Why did you do that?

249
00:21:47.764 --> 00:21:50.892
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Hey man, it's Sean. My name is Sean.

250
00:21:50.976 --> 00:21:53.895
- That's what I said, right?
- That's what I heard.

251
00:21:53.979 --> 00:21:55.731
- Right?
- Whatever.

252
00:21:55.814 --> 00:21:58.275
Georgie, we're gonna
destroy you this year.

253
00:21:58.358 --> 00:21:59.943
Because what?

254
00:22:00.027 --> 00:22:02.195
We haven't lost in how long?

255
00:22:02.863 --> 00:22:04.323
Oh yeah, that's right.

256
00:22:05.449 --> 00:22:06.908
- Yeah. Mmm.
- Wow.

257
00:22:06.992 --> 00:22:08.201
- Good ear.
- A long time.

258
00:22:08.285 --> 00:22:10.704
Maybe you'll be one of my Apostles, Will.

259
00:22:10.787 --> 00:22:11.787
- Really?
- Yeah.

260
00:22:12.164 --> 00:22:14.249
If you have Apostles,
doesn't that make you...

261
00:22:14.333 --> 00:22:17.169
- Winners! Yes!
- Okay, got it.

262
00:22:17.252 --> 00:22:20.088
So, you're a team of Apostles. Got it.

263
00:22:20.172 --> 00:22:23.884
For a second there I thought you might
have an over inflated sense of self.

264
00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:27.637
The thing is,
I'm not sure I'm brave enough

265
00:22:27.721 --> 00:22:30.849
to pull off one of those t-shirts
in public, I'll have to pass.

266
00:22:30.932 --> 00:22:35.645
Oh. That's a shame
because I sell these t-shirts

267
00:22:35.729 --> 00:22:37.647
to raise money
for a cause close to my heart.

268
00:22:37.731 --> 00:22:40.317
- I think that's him on there.
- On that narwhal.

269
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:42.152
Anyways, your team's not a choice.

270
00:22:42.235 --> 00:22:44.613
We'll see what happens
tonight at the tribunal.

271
00:22:45.447 --> 00:22:46.447
Can't wait.

272
00:22:46.823 --> 00:22:49.534
Great. Awesome.
I'll see you gentlemen tonight.

273
00:22:49.618 --> 00:22:51.119
- See you tonight.
- You will.

274
00:22:51.203 --> 00:22:53.163
- Apostles out.
- See you there.

275
00:22:53.246 --> 00:22:54.081
Great!

276
00:22:54.164 --> 00:22:57.376
Hoo-rah!

277
00:22:58.502 --> 00:23:00.837
- Okay, let's be on our way.
- Will.

278
00:23:01.421 --> 00:23:03.173
What is this tribunal thing?

279
00:23:05.217 --> 00:23:09.262
We're gathered here tonight
on this hallowed ground

280
00:23:10.639 --> 00:23:15.519
beneath the great moon and stars,
to honor an age old tradition.

281
00:23:16.978 --> 00:23:19.689
Welcome to the tribunal!

282
00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:32.661
Newbies! Rise!

283
00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:38.041
From this day forth,

284
00:23:39.167 --> 00:23:43.130
you'll be part of your tribe,
and your tribe will be part of you.

285
00:23:44.297 --> 00:23:45.507
And you forever

286
00:23:46.299 --> 00:23:47.634
will be part of us all.

287
00:23:50.011 --> 00:23:51.011
Come forth!

288
00:23:58.145 --> 00:23:59.145
Crimson Angel!

289
00:24:08.029 --> 00:24:09.197
Azure Apostle!

290
00:24:13.785 --> 00:24:14.785
Whoo!

291
00:24:17.372 --> 00:24:18.665
Crimson Angel!

292
00:24:24.629 --> 00:24:26.006
Good to meet you, Will.

293
00:24:26.798 --> 00:24:27.632
You too.

294
00:24:27.716 --> 00:24:28.716
All right.

295
00:24:31.761 --> 00:24:33.096
Verdes Maximus!

296
00:24:39.352 --> 00:24:41.313
I pulled some strings.
Pretty cool, huh?

297
00:24:41.396 --> 00:24:43.190
You're one of us now.

298
00:24:43.273 --> 00:24:44.399
Azure Apostle!

299
00:24:59.789 --> 00:25:01.708
No!

300
00:25:01.791 --> 00:25:04.169
We're gonna have a lot of fun this week.

301
00:25:28.944 --> 00:25:30.320
All right!

302
00:25:43.792 --> 00:25:45.710
Awesome!

303
00:25:46.670 --> 00:25:48.713
Greatest week ever, right?

304
00:25:49.381 --> 00:25:50.549
Well, you'll get there.

305
00:26:02.852 --> 00:26:04.980
All right, let's go!

306
00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:18.285
Yes, God loves us all equally.

307
00:26:18.368 --> 00:26:20.078
Let the games begin!

308
00:26:30.547 --> 00:26:32.090
Good morning, campers.

309
00:26:32.173 --> 00:26:36.011
It's a beautiful sunny day.
Everybody up. Everybody moving.

310
00:26:36.094 --> 00:26:39.097
It's time to get this party grooving.

311
00:26:39.180 --> 00:26:42.642
As you know, another year
of Warrior Games is at hand.

312
00:26:42.726 --> 00:26:45.103
Will the Apostles hold onto their lead?

313
00:26:45.186 --> 00:26:49.482
Or will another team rise
from the ashes and claim their throne?

314
00:26:49.566 --> 00:26:53.111
Good morning, campers.
It is a beautiful sunny day.

315
00:26:53.194 --> 00:26:57.198
Everybody up. Everybody moving.
It's time to get this party grooving.

316
00:26:57.282 --> 00:26:58.617
Just make it stop.

317
00:26:59.743 --> 00:27:02.412
- Hello. Earth to Will.
- Go away.

318
00:27:02.495 --> 00:27:04.122
We get to kick total butt today.

319
00:27:04.205 --> 00:27:07.083
Finally show Sean
and his mini-me's how Jedis get it done.

320
00:27:08.418 --> 00:27:12.380
- It's gonna be epic.
- No, it's not going to be epic.

321
00:27:12.464 --> 00:27:15.967
I'm 17.6 miles from civilization
and surrounded by Jesus freaks.

322
00:27:16.968 --> 00:27:20.847
Wow. I feel like I should be offended
but I'm actually just impressed

323
00:27:20.930 --> 00:27:23.266
with your geographical skills. Like,

324
00:27:23.350 --> 00:27:24.851
did you just know that?

325
00:27:27.187 --> 00:27:28.187
Rule number one:

326
00:27:28.938 --> 00:27:30.607
Always have an exit plan.

327
00:27:30.690 --> 00:27:33.151
- That's rule number one?
- Yes, it is.

328
00:27:33.234 --> 00:27:35.487
Problem is,
all roads lead to juvie this time.

329
00:27:37.030 --> 00:27:39.741
Yeah, but this time you got a George.

330
00:27:40.408 --> 00:27:43.953
He's not going to let you leave.
Right? I need you for the talent show.

331
00:27:44.037 --> 00:27:47.082
You're what I need
to bring the performance over the top.

332
00:27:47.165 --> 00:27:50.460
- And it's gonna be epic.
- Please stop saying that.

333
00:27:50.543 --> 00:27:54.255
Well, it's true.
I'll quit if you quit with the "boo-hoo,

334
00:27:54.339 --> 00:27:58.301
I'd rather be anywhere than this place
because I'm so broody and cool."

335
00:27:58.385 --> 00:28:00.428
It's not a good look, even I know that.

336
00:28:01.930 --> 00:28:05.850
Look, you have a chance to do
something really solid this week.

337
00:28:07.394 --> 00:28:09.521
Help me win for the first time in my life.

338
00:28:09.604 --> 00:28:10.897
Bonus, hang with Avery.

339
00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:14.359
And, who knows,
maybe you'll have a little bit of fun.

340
00:28:14.442 --> 00:28:15.527
Like, by accident?

341
00:28:16.027 --> 00:28:17.445
So, stop whining.

342
00:28:17.987 --> 00:28:19.072
Suck it up.

343
00:28:27.038 --> 00:28:30.375
- That was a pretty solid pep talk, George.
- Thank you.

344
00:28:31.543 --> 00:28:32.669
Did you practice that?

345
00:28:33.336 --> 00:28:35.880
I did. Was the singing too much?
I couldn't decide.

346
00:28:35.964 --> 00:28:38.049
- No, that's what got me.
- The singing?

347
00:28:38.133 --> 00:28:39.592
Nice.

348
00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:44.222
Want some Ovaltine? Apple Jacks?

349
00:28:44.305 --> 00:28:46.516
- No, I'm good. I got Twizzlers.
- Nice.

350
00:28:52.647 --> 00:28:54.858
Why would you get more of this?

351
00:28:54.941 --> 00:28:56.651
I like it. It's camp.

352
00:28:56.735 --> 00:28:59.112
- It's gross, is what it is.
- You're supposed to get a bun.

353
00:28:59.195 --> 00:29:00.238
All right.

354
00:29:00.321 --> 00:29:01.321
All right!

355
00:29:03.366 --> 00:29:04.492
Five minutes!

356
00:29:05.660 --> 00:29:07.036
Five minutes!

357
00:29:07.537 --> 00:29:08.955
Five minutes!

358
00:29:09.038 --> 00:29:12.500
Five minutes!

359
00:29:12.584 --> 00:29:14.384
- What's going on?
- You're not gonna like it.

360
00:29:14.419 --> 00:29:17.797
All right! The people have spoken.

361
00:29:18.798 --> 00:29:20.592
- Will Hawkins!
- There it is.

362
00:29:20.675 --> 00:29:23.094
It's time for your five minutes of fame.

363
00:29:23.178 --> 00:29:24.679
- Five minutes?
- Get there.

364
00:29:24.763 --> 00:29:26.556
Five minutes!

365
00:29:26.639 --> 00:29:28.057
Five minutes!

366
00:29:28.141 --> 00:29:30.059
Five minutes!

367
00:29:30.143 --> 00:29:32.979
- Get up there.
- Okay, I'll do it.

368
00:29:33.062 --> 00:29:35.899
- Let's give it up for the new kid!
- Wish me luck.

369
00:29:38.276 --> 00:29:39.611
I believe in you!

370
00:29:39.694 --> 00:29:41.821
The name is William Hawkins.

371
00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:45.450
The game is five minutes of fame.

372
00:29:45.533 --> 00:29:50.205
And the name of the game is to find out
who the mysterious new kid really is.

373
00:29:50.288 --> 00:29:51.288
Mysterious? Huh.

374
00:29:53.166 --> 00:29:55.710
Okay, all right.

375
00:29:56.628 --> 00:29:57.504
Bring it on.

376
00:29:57.587 --> 00:29:58.671
Favorite color?

377
00:29:59.631 --> 00:30:00.632
Green, of course.

378
00:30:03.134 --> 00:30:04.844
- Profession?
- Teenager.

379
00:30:04.928 --> 00:30:06.638
- Favorite movie?
- Twilight.

380
00:30:06.721 --> 00:30:08.723
You good at sports?

381
00:30:08.807 --> 00:30:10.600
If awesome is good then yeah.

382
00:30:12.602 --> 00:30:14.121
- Celebrity crush?
- Bella Swan.

383
00:30:14.145 --> 00:30:15.855
Real crush?

384
00:30:15.939 --> 00:30:18.483
I'm still going with Bella.

385
00:30:18.566 --> 00:30:20.085
- Biggest regret?
- Sitting here.

386
00:30:20.109 --> 00:30:21.486
Favorite book of the Bible?

387
00:30:25.782 --> 00:30:28.701
Ah, man, you know,
I-I couldn't pick just one.

388
00:30:29.244 --> 00:30:30.829
Oh, I totally get that.

389
00:30:33.081 --> 00:30:34.082
Who's your hero?

390
00:30:35.625 --> 00:30:36.751
My dad.

391
00:30:36.835 --> 00:30:38.586
Your favorite person?

392
00:30:39.963 --> 00:30:41.005
My mom.

393
00:30:42.966 --> 00:30:45.760
Okay, all right!

394
00:30:46.302 --> 00:30:48.263
Let's give it up for the new kid, huh?

395
00:30:51.349 --> 00:30:52.809
All right, who's next?

396
00:30:52.892 --> 00:30:54.894
How about Georgie boy?
I believe in you, cuz.

397
00:30:54.978 --> 00:30:57.605
- I don't know!
- Come on! Come on up here.

398
00:30:58.690 --> 00:31:00.191
George! George! George!

399
00:31:00.275 --> 00:31:04.153
- Okay, okay.
- George! George!

400
00:31:04.237 --> 00:31:06.406
All right! Okay.

401
00:31:06.489 --> 00:31:07.991
- You're welcome.
- Will.

402
00:31:10.201 --> 00:31:11.201
Thanks a lot.

403
00:31:13.788 --> 00:31:17.125
- Whatever happened, I swear it wasn't me.
- Oh, you can relax.

404
00:31:17.208 --> 00:31:19.794
I don't believe for a second
you're a Twilight fan.

405
00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:20.879
You don't seem the type.

406
00:31:20.962 --> 00:31:23.006
- Don't judge a book by its cover.
- I never do.

407
00:31:23.089 --> 00:31:25.550
I just wanna say
I'm glad you're here, Will.

408
00:31:25.633 --> 00:31:28.803
That's it. So I called you out here.
Glad you're here.

409
00:31:30.013 --> 00:31:31.389
Well, thanks.

410
00:31:32.181 --> 00:31:35.268
Hey, by the way, what's with the name?
Aweegaway?

411
00:31:35.351 --> 00:31:37.395
Yeah, no, it's Aweegaway.

412
00:31:37.478 --> 00:31:40.064
You guys are taking a week away
to hang out with us.

413
00:31:41.232 --> 00:31:42.984
Oh, yeah, that makes more sense.

414
00:31:43.067 --> 00:31:47.238
And bonus, every once in a while,
somebody finds out they're a week away

415
00:31:47.322 --> 00:31:49.490
from an experience
that changed everything for them.

416
00:31:49.574 --> 00:31:50.617
My favorite part.

417
00:31:53.244 --> 00:31:57.832
Here I was thinking you were a funny guy
who was a little too into Braveheart.

418
00:31:57.916 --> 00:32:00.710
You're right, I am a funny guy
and I do love Braveheart.

419
00:32:00.793 --> 00:32:03.838
- But don't judge a book by its cover.
- Touché.

420
00:32:03.922 --> 00:32:06.466
One last thing.
Don't put my camp on Craigslist.

421
00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:10.553
- I won't.
- Okay, thank you. Well, it's time.

422
00:32:10.637 --> 00:32:11.971
For what?

423
00:32:12.055 --> 00:32:13.806
Warrior Games, baby!

424
00:32:16.768 --> 00:32:18.686
- Wow.
- Warrior Games!

425
00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:22.398
- Hear ya.
- Man, is that Will Hawkins, the new kid?

426
00:32:22.482 --> 00:32:25.360
Thanks a lot.
You set the bar high in there.

427
00:32:25.443 --> 00:32:28.488
- I'm sure you were great.
- If awesome is good then yeah.

428
00:32:28.571 --> 00:32:29.989
Oh my gosh.

429
00:32:30.073 --> 00:32:32.283
Everyone's talking about you
and Sean hates it.

430
00:32:32.367 --> 00:32:33.368
- Will!
- Tragic.

431
00:32:33.451 --> 00:32:35.954
- That was so impressive.
- Oh, thank you.

432
00:32:36.037 --> 00:32:40.041
Yeah, I mean, anyone can answer
questions, but it is about to get real.

433
00:32:40.124 --> 00:32:42.001
Whoo!

434
00:32:42.085 --> 00:32:44.379
Warrior Games, baby!

435
00:32:44.462 --> 00:32:45.296
What he said.

436
00:32:45.380 --> 00:32:46.798
- Whoo!
- That's right.

437
00:32:46.881 --> 00:32:50.551
- You're gonna beat the blob this year.
- That's because I love the blob.

438
00:32:50.635 --> 00:32:53.513
- This girl loves the blob.
- I do love the blob.

439
00:32:53.596 --> 00:32:56.099
- That's why I do it, Sean.
- I love the blob too.

440
00:32:56.182 --> 00:32:57.976
- Really?
- I do.

441
00:32:58.059 --> 00:33:02.230
- You love the blob? I thought you...
- George, you know me. I love that thing.

442
00:33:02.313 --> 00:33:04.357
- Great.
- My friends call me "blobtastic."

443
00:33:04.440 --> 00:33:07.318
- That's cool.
- Really? You like can't get them to stop?

444
00:33:07.402 --> 00:33:11.030
I've tried, but they just seem
too overwhelmed by my skills.

445
00:33:11.698 --> 00:33:12.991
Of course.

446
00:33:13.074 --> 00:33:14.409
Ah, well, look,

447
00:33:14.492 --> 00:33:17.620
don't feel bad because when I beat you
I won't think any less of you.

448
00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:19.664
Okay.

449
00:33:19.747 --> 00:33:21.416
Mr. Blobtastic.

450
00:33:21.499 --> 00:33:22.834
You can call me Will.

451
00:33:24.252 --> 00:33:27.505
Uh, eh... Bye. Bye, George.

452
00:33:29.465 --> 00:33:30.967
I didn't know you blobbed.

453
00:33:31.050 --> 00:33:34.095
If we go now we could get
practice jumps before anyone else.

454
00:33:34.178 --> 00:33:35.263
You wanna? Come on!

455
00:33:35.346 --> 00:33:38.975
Wait, back up, jumps? You didn't say
there were gonna be jumps.

456
00:33:40.018 --> 00:33:41.018
George!

457
00:33:46.149 --> 00:33:47.316
Time to fly.

458
00:33:48.067 --> 00:33:50.069
Can you give me
something extra on the jump?

459
00:33:50.153 --> 00:33:52.071
The further I go, the higher we score.

460
00:33:53.281 --> 00:33:54.574
- Hello?
- Huh?

461
00:33:55.658 --> 00:33:57.243
Dude, that's pretty tall.

462
00:33:57.326 --> 00:33:59.912
Yeah, it's the blob.
Wait, have you never...

463
00:34:00.955 --> 00:34:01.955
No.

464
00:34:03.416 --> 00:34:05.585
Yeah, great. Well, Blobtastic,

465
00:34:06.544 --> 00:34:07.544
today's the day.

466
00:37:09.769 --> 00:37:13.189
Get ready,
next up is an epic dodgeball face off.

467
00:37:21.489 --> 00:37:22.573
Come on, Presley!

468
00:37:26.160 --> 00:37:30.039
Hey! Oh, not cool.

469
00:37:31.040 --> 00:37:33.209
Oh! Sorry. Didn't see you.

470
00:37:42.426 --> 00:37:43.761
We can do this!

471
00:37:45.137 --> 00:37:47.598
Oh!

472
00:37:47.682 --> 00:37:49.058
It's okay. You're fine.

473
00:37:49.141 --> 00:37:51.435
Hey, good work.

474
00:37:54.522 --> 00:37:55.648
Eye on the prize!

475
00:38:17.253 --> 00:38:19.130
Presley!

476
00:38:19.213 --> 00:38:23.301
No!

477
00:38:31.267 --> 00:38:32.727
- I'll be right back.
- Wow!

478
00:38:34.395 --> 00:38:36.230
Oh, poor baby.

479
00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:39.692
- Try this.
- Thank you so much.

480
00:38:39.775 --> 00:38:41.152
Oh.

481
00:38:41.235 --> 00:38:42.320
It's cold.

482
00:38:42.403 --> 00:38:44.989
- Let me know if you need anything else.
- You're an angel.

483
00:38:45.072 --> 00:38:46.073
Thank you.

484
00:38:51.579 --> 00:38:54.081
She's right there. Just go check on her.

485
00:38:55.041 --> 00:38:56.834
- Come on, you can do this.
- No.

486
00:38:57.501 --> 00:38:58.336
George.

487
00:38:58.419 --> 00:39:01.005
It's really not that bad, you know. Sorry.

488
00:39:01.088 --> 00:39:04.383
I have a bag of peas on my face, Avery.

489
00:39:04.467 --> 00:39:06.052
Yeah, but your hair...

490
00:39:07.053 --> 00:39:08.554
it's never looked better.

491
00:39:09.430 --> 00:39:10.430
Really?

492
00:39:11.640 --> 00:39:15.603
No, it's actually really frizzy
and it's a little flat.

493
00:39:20.816 --> 00:39:24.070
- George, what are you doing?
- I can't go out there, forget it.

494
00:39:24.153 --> 00:39:26.655
Stop pacing. Please.

495
00:39:26.739 --> 00:39:27.656
Stop!

496
00:39:27.740 --> 00:39:31.494
You just don't understand.
I'll never be the guy who gets the girl.

497
00:39:31.577 --> 00:39:33.204
I'm Duckie. What can I say?

498
00:39:33.287 --> 00:39:35.831
What? You are the cool guy, George.

499
00:39:36.499 --> 00:39:38.501
- You're kinda the coolest.
- I'm a sucker.

500
00:39:39.251 --> 00:39:42.421
You gotta go out there and get her.
This is your moment.

501
00:39:42.505 --> 00:39:45.091
- Like one of those Jeff Hughes movies.
- John Hughes.

502
00:39:45.174 --> 00:39:47.802
- John Hughes.
- That's it! You have to John Hughes me.

503
00:39:49.387 --> 00:39:50.262
What?

504
00:39:50.346 --> 00:39:52.640
John Hughes me. The makeover montage.

505
00:39:52.723 --> 00:39:56.560
We go to the mall, you get me
a leather jacket, jeans with rips in 'em,

506
00:39:56.644 --> 00:39:58.729
and killer shades. It works every time.

507
00:39:58.813 --> 00:40:00.940
Come on, just do it.

508
00:40:01.023 --> 00:40:02.733
All right, I'll see what I can do.

509
00:40:11.075 --> 00:40:12.284
Now go get the girl.

510
00:40:14.161 --> 00:40:16.205
That was a really quick montage.

511
00:41:52.676 --> 00:41:53.677
Super nope.

512
00:41:56.555 --> 00:41:59.892
Good morning, campers.
It's a beautiful sunny day.

513
00:41:59.975 --> 00:42:04.897
Everybody up. Everybody moving.
It's time to get this party grooving.

514
00:42:05.564 --> 00:42:09.985
Afternoon water sports
have been postpone d due to umm...

515
00:42:10.069 --> 00:42:12.071
uh... but we're cleaning up.

516
00:42:12.154 --> 00:42:14.490
Side note: Chef Lisa's spicy chili

517
00:42:14.573 --> 00:42:17.159
is off the lunch menu
for the remainder of the week.

518
00:42:32.132 --> 00:42:33.259
That's beautiful.

519
00:42:36.387 --> 00:42:37.638
Oh, sorry, I...

520
00:42:38.180 --> 00:42:39.682
I was just walking.

521
00:42:39.765 --> 00:42:41.684
- I didn't mean to...
- No, it's cool.

522
00:42:42.685 --> 00:42:44.812
I thought I'd come here,
watch the sunrise.

523
00:42:44.895 --> 00:42:45.938
Mh.

524
00:42:46.021 --> 00:42:48.566
And George is a little perky for me
in the morning.

525
00:42:48.649 --> 00:42:49.984
So...

526
00:42:50.859 --> 00:42:51.859
Yeah.

527
00:42:52.987 --> 00:42:53.987
Is that, um...

528
00:42:54.488 --> 00:42:55.739
something that you wrote?

529
00:42:56.824 --> 00:42:59.577
Uh, just a little something
I've been working on.

530
00:42:59.660 --> 00:43:02.913
So he's Mr. Blobtastic
and he plays the guitar.

531
00:43:02.997 --> 00:43:04.707
That is pretty impressive.

532
00:43:05.958 --> 00:43:08.544
All right, I'm up here
writing moody sunrise songs.

533
00:43:09.044 --> 00:43:10.087
What's your excuse?

534
00:43:13.382 --> 00:43:17.803
You know, it's kind of a personal thing,
but if you wanted to, you could come.

535
00:43:18.846 --> 00:43:20.306
Pass up a mystery outing?

536
00:43:20.931 --> 00:43:22.016
Let's do it.

537
00:43:29.815 --> 00:43:31.025
Just over here.

538
00:43:32.526 --> 00:43:34.945
Are you taking me to some secret hideout?

539
00:43:35.029 --> 00:43:36.780
Sort of.

540
00:43:37.698 --> 00:43:39.533
- Should I be alarmed?
- No!

541
00:43:39.617 --> 00:43:41.785
Okay, just checking basics.

542
00:43:42.911 --> 00:43:44.913
Y'know, I'm kinda a big deal at camp,

543
00:43:44.997 --> 00:43:48.125
so if I go missing,
people will come looking.

544
00:43:48.208 --> 00:43:49.460
- Will they?
- Mmm-hmm.

545
00:43:49.543 --> 00:43:50.543
Really?

546
00:44:07.061 --> 00:44:08.061
Wow.

547
00:44:09.063 --> 00:44:10.564
Pretty amazing, huh?

548
00:44:12.900 --> 00:44:14.276
I come here every year.

549
00:44:15.069 --> 00:44:18.238
It is pretty much
my favorite place on the planet.

550
00:44:19.990 --> 00:44:21.575
I can see why.

551
00:44:23.369 --> 00:44:24.828
When I was little my, um...

552
00:44:26.372 --> 00:44:27.456
my mom, she got sick.

553
00:44:28.123 --> 00:44:31.335
And so my dad and I
wanted to create a place

554
00:44:31.919 --> 00:44:35.130
that was magical for her
when she wasn't in the hospital, so...

555
00:44:36.048 --> 00:44:37.048
we made this.

556
00:44:39.635 --> 00:44:43.305
My mom, her favorite were the butterflies.
There are some now,

557
00:44:43.389 --> 00:44:46.141
but you come back in the spring,
I'm telling you, you...

558
00:44:46.809 --> 00:44:48.102
you would not believe it.

559
00:44:52.731 --> 00:44:54.983
Y'know, it's been almost eleven years.

560
00:44:57.444 --> 00:44:58.570
But she's still here.

561
00:45:01.115 --> 00:45:02.115
Doesn't it hurt?

562
00:45:04.243 --> 00:45:05.243
Being here?

563
00:45:09.039 --> 00:45:10.039
Well, yeah.

564
00:45:11.417 --> 00:45:14.086
Of course, I miss her, every day, but...

565
00:45:16.004 --> 00:45:17.923
I know that it's just temporary.

566
00:45:19.842 --> 00:45:22.344
- So you'll see her again?
- A hundred percent.

567
00:45:22.886 --> 00:45:24.596
A hundred percent? Wow.

568
00:45:24.680 --> 00:45:27.474
I mean, I guess I don't,
I don't know-know that, but...

569
00:45:29.518 --> 00:45:31.311
Yeah, no, I just choose to believe.

570
00:45:32.104 --> 00:45:33.647
I mean that's faith, right?

571
00:45:36.900 --> 00:45:37.985
What about you?

572
00:45:39.111 --> 00:45:40.111
What?

573
00:45:41.405 --> 00:45:42.573
Oh yeah.

574
00:45:43.115 --> 00:45:44.700
Uh, me too.

575
00:45:45.659 --> 00:45:47.119
Yeah, I was just testing you.

576
00:45:47.870 --> 00:45:49.246
Right.

577
00:45:50.664 --> 00:45:52.166
Okay, well, how did I do?

578
00:45:53.125 --> 00:45:54.334
Nailed it. Of course.

579
00:46:01.008 --> 00:46:02.426
You're pretty perfect, aren't you?

580
00:46:05.929 --> 00:46:06.929
No.

581
00:46:07.264 --> 00:46:08.265
No, I'm not.

582
00:46:08.348 --> 00:46:11.977
- It's okay, you can admit it.
- No, I can't though, because I'm not.

583
00:46:16.148 --> 00:46:18.150
Look, to be honest with you,

584
00:46:18.233 --> 00:46:21.570
and I know you didn't mean it
in a bad way or anything, it's just...

585
00:46:22.905 --> 00:46:23.947
I hate that word.

586
00:46:25.157 --> 00:46:28.452
Y'know, perfect, it's just impossible.

587
00:46:28.535 --> 00:46:32.498
It's like I find myself doing this thing
I know that I shouldn't but,

588
00:46:33.165 --> 00:46:35.918
I'm, like, trying to be what everybody
expects me to be,

589
00:46:37.085 --> 00:46:39.588
and it is exhausting.

590
00:46:40.464 --> 00:46:42.174
Well, I didn't mean it like that.

591
00:46:42.841 --> 00:46:43.841
I know, I...

592
00:46:48.347 --> 00:46:51.141
It just seems
like you have it all figured out.

593
00:49:50.278 --> 00:49:51.278
See?

594
00:49:52.489 --> 00:49:53.489
I was right.

595
00:49:55.158 --> 00:49:56.158
You're perfect.

596
00:49:58.078 --> 00:49:59.079
So, um...

597
00:49:59.830 --> 00:50:01.081
where do you live, again?

598
00:50:01.832 --> 00:50:03.792
Y'know, after, after the summer?

599
00:50:05.919 --> 00:50:09.297
- I live in New York with my older brother.
- Hmm.

600
00:50:10.298 --> 00:50:13.510
We're super close.
I'm really lucky to have him.

601
00:50:16.096 --> 00:50:18.140
I thought you said you lived in Philly.

602
00:50:20.308 --> 00:50:22.394
Uh-oh! You are in trouble.

603
00:50:23.311 --> 00:50:24.311
What do you mean?

604
00:50:37.492 --> 00:50:40.412
I love the smell
of paintball in the morning!

605
00:50:40.495 --> 00:50:43.832
- Your dad is really into this.
- Yeah. Like father like daughter.

606
00:50:43.915 --> 00:50:46.877
This is sudden death!
The surviving team

607
00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:48.045
wins the day!

608
00:50:48.128 --> 00:50:51.131
Okay, David, you do realize
they're kids, right?

609
00:50:51.214 --> 00:50:52.507
- I know.
- Okay.

610
00:50:53.175 --> 00:50:55.218
Charlie! No more head shots.

611
00:50:55.969 --> 00:50:58.805
And remember, watch your six.

612
00:50:58.889 --> 00:51:00.515
Not the 666.

613
00:51:01.016 --> 00:51:05.437
No, I was... The six is your back.
'Cause if you say twelve it would be...

614
00:51:05.520 --> 00:51:08.482
I hope you know how to shoot that thing.

615
00:51:08.565 --> 00:51:11.735
- Not the devil!
- No, this is not a Biblical term at all.

616
00:51:11.818 --> 00:51:13.487
Okay. All right, gotcha.

617
00:51:13.570 --> 00:51:14.821
Move out!

618
00:51:14.905 --> 00:51:17.699
- Move it!
- Jesus loves you!

619
00:51:17.783 --> 00:51:18.784
Move it!

620
00:51:18.867 --> 00:51:20.160
Slay 'em all!

621
00:51:20.243 --> 00:51:24.247
- Charlie's really enthusiastic.
- Yeah, we've got to call his parents.

622
00:51:24.831 --> 00:51:29.711
All right, Apostles, listen up.
It is beyond go time.

623
00:51:29.795 --> 00:51:32.631
Now just go out there, okay,
and do your best.

624
00:51:32.714 --> 00:51:34.674
Now, I believe in you.

625
00:51:34.758 --> 00:51:37.761
This is our year, 'cause we have
something they don't have.

626
00:51:37.844 --> 00:51:39.137
We have Will.

627
00:51:39.221 --> 00:51:41.973
I want the new kid taken out first.
Understand?

628
00:51:42.057 --> 00:51:44.392
Do you think they all know
what Apocalypse Now is?

629
00:51:44.476 --> 00:51:46.728
I don't even know
what Apocalypse Now is, David.

630
00:51:46.812 --> 00:51:48.730
- Now, what are we?
- Red hot!

631
00:51:48.814 --> 00:51:50.607
Sorry, I can't hear you. What?

632
00:51:50.690 --> 00:51:51.817
Verdes Maximus!

633
00:51:51.900 --> 00:51:53.401
What are we gonna do?

634
00:51:53.485 --> 00:51:55.028
- Destroy.
- Yes.

635
00:51:55.112 --> 00:51:56.154
Now hands in!

636
00:51:56.238 --> 00:51:57.155
Masks down.

637
00:51:57.239 --> 00:51:58.532
On three. Um...

638
00:51:58.615 --> 00:52:01.159
- After three.
- After three. Yes. Thank you.

639
00:52:01.243 --> 00:52:03.578
Green machine. One, two, three:

640
00:52:03.662 --> 00:52:05.664
Let's go!

641
00:52:24.141 --> 00:52:25.141
Pull harder!

642
00:52:41.533 --> 00:52:43.451
- What are you doing?
- Go. Back.

643
00:53:09.352 --> 00:53:11.897
- I'm open!
- Not anymore!

644
00:53:13.231 --> 00:53:16.193
Somebody call heaven!
These Angels got wings!

645
00:54:06.076 --> 00:54:07.244
Yay!

646
00:54:08.370 --> 00:54:10.538
Oh, that's gotta hurt.

647
00:54:12.123 --> 00:54:15.835
Points are adding up and it's
not looking good for the Apostles.

648
00:54:27.264 --> 00:54:28.848
What are you doing? Get up!

649
00:54:31.768 --> 00:54:32.768
George!

650
00:54:38.108 --> 00:54:40.318
Wow.

651
00:54:40.402 --> 00:54:45.657
That was the nicest/weirdest thing
anyone's ever done for me.

652
00:54:45.740 --> 00:54:48.285
You're welcome, Georgie.

653
00:54:48.368 --> 00:54:50.287
- Let's go.
- Paintball sucks.

654
00:54:50.370 --> 00:54:52.205
I know.

655
00:54:52.289 --> 00:54:53.290
Charlie!

656
00:54:53.373 --> 00:54:56.126
I will come after you
with the wrath of God!

657
00:54:56.209 --> 00:54:58.044
- I'm not playing, Charlie!
- Hey, hey.

658
00:54:58.128 --> 00:54:59.254
What?

659
00:54:59.337 --> 00:55:01.548
You do realize they're children,
don't you?

660
00:55:02.424 --> 00:55:03.758
Charlie!

661
00:55:20.650 --> 00:55:22.861
You're going down. Three.

662
00:55:22.944 --> 00:55:23.987
Two.

663
00:55:24.070 --> 00:55:25.238
One!

664
00:55:32.037 --> 00:55:34.357
- Why aren't you shooting me?
- Why aren't you shooting me?

665
00:55:34.998 --> 00:55:38.585
We're surrounded. If we reload
and shoot each other then Sean wins.

666
00:55:38.668 --> 00:55:41.713
Okay. What are you proposing?

667
00:55:44.424 --> 00:55:45.508
Temporary truce?

668
00:55:47.677 --> 00:55:48.677
Okay.

669
00:55:50.347 --> 00:55:52.474
Let's Mr. and Mrs. Smith this thing.

670
00:55:52.557 --> 00:55:54.100
Yes! Yes!

671
00:55:54.684 --> 00:55:55.727
What is that again?

672
00:55:55.810 --> 00:56:00.023
What? Y'know, it's like a movie.
Like Mr... No?

673
00:56:00.690 --> 00:56:03.193
- Just follow my lead, okay?
- Yeah, here you go.

674
00:56:03.276 --> 00:56:05.987
No, Will, that's yours too.
You're gonna shoot both.

675
00:56:06.071 --> 00:56:07.781
Okay.

676
00:56:12.577 --> 00:56:13.995
We got 'em, Apostles.

677
00:56:14.079 --> 00:56:18.249
On the count of three. One, two, three!

678
00:56:53.284 --> 00:56:54.828
Hey! Ow! Ow!

679
00:56:54.911 --> 00:56:57.080
Ow! That is so against the rules!

680
00:56:58.540 --> 00:57:00.083
Ow! Stop! I'm down!

681
00:57:03.086 --> 00:57:05.422
- Wow. That is so wrong.
- Aww.

682
00:57:05.505 --> 00:57:08.383
I told you, Will, I'm competitive.

683
00:57:09.676 --> 00:57:11.177
Excuse me boys.

684
00:57:11.261 --> 00:57:14.305
That's it! Crimson Angels are the winner!

685
00:57:14.389 --> 00:57:17.142
Looks like we're both losers today.

686
00:57:17.225 --> 00:57:18.351
Just go.

687
00:57:18.435 --> 00:57:21.020
Part of me is proud,
and part of me is neutral.

688
00:57:21.104 --> 00:57:23.523
I think we got a barn burner!

689
00:57:23.606 --> 00:57:25.650
Verdes Maximus is in second place!

690
00:57:25.733 --> 00:57:28.278
That's my baby!
He came from my womb.

691
00:57:28.361 --> 00:57:32.449
And in third place just a couple
of points down the Azure Apostles.

692
00:57:32.532 --> 00:57:36.035
Oh, no, no. This doesn't happen.

693
00:57:36.119 --> 00:57:37.162
Third place!

694
00:57:37.245 --> 00:57:39.622
I pray. I give blood. What is happening?

695
00:57:39.706 --> 00:57:41.833
I'm an Apostle. I went to the Arctic

696
00:57:41.916 --> 00:57:44.377
and I spent two months
freezing my buttocks off

697
00:57:44.461 --> 00:57:46.796
to come back here and we lose.

698
00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:51.468
We lose to some guy,
George's cousin. Who is that guy?

699
00:57:52.218 --> 00:57:56.806
Hello, Mr. Godzilla. That looks like
a tasty Twizzler you have in your mouth.

700
00:57:57.307 --> 00:58:00.727
Oh! Thank you so much.

701
00:58:01.478 --> 00:58:03.396
I'm going to keep this Twizzler.

702
00:58:22.373 --> 00:58:23.583
You win.

703
00:58:25.418 --> 00:58:27.962
- We suck!
- Why can't we? Why are we so bad at this?

704
00:58:32.467 --> 00:58:36.095
- Finished it.
- Oh wow, I'm ashamed.

705
00:58:37.430 --> 00:58:39.682
Life moves pretty fast.

706
00:58:39.766 --> 00:58:42.018
If you don't stop and look around
once in a while,

707
00:58:42.101 --> 00:58:43.186
you could miss it.

708
00:58:43.269 --> 00:58:44.938
- So good.
- Dude, it's a classic.

709
00:58:45.021 --> 00:58:47.398
You know?
This camp thing's not that bad.

710
00:58:47.482 --> 00:58:49.317
You ain't seen nothing yet.

711
00:58:53.530 --> 00:58:55.865
I just have
one simple thing to say.

712
00:58:56.658 --> 00:58:58.076
I don't know all of you...

713
00:58:59.911 --> 00:59:01.496
certainly not as well as I'd like to.

714
00:59:03.081 --> 00:59:04.207
But God does.

715
00:59:05.500 --> 00:59:09.087
He knows everything about each
and every one of you here tonight.

716
00:59:10.004 --> 00:59:13.091
I don't know much, but this much I do.

717
00:59:14.634 --> 00:59:15.634
He's a fan.

718
00:59:21.975 --> 00:59:23.101
I don't know much.

719
00:59:25.770 --> 00:59:27.188
But I...

720
00:59:27.897 --> 00:59:30.149
- Err... uh...
- But this much I do.

721
00:59:33.861 --> 00:59:37.323
Seeing George hit that superman pose
trying to save a certain someone.

722
00:59:39.033 --> 00:59:40.118
That was, uh...

723
00:59:41.995 --> 00:59:43.496
That was pretty cool, man.

724
00:59:44.747 --> 00:59:45.999
That was pretty cool.

725
00:59:49.961 --> 00:59:51.004
- Thanks.
- Yeah.

726
00:59:51.087 --> 00:59:53.715
Well, I don't know much,
but this much I do.

727
00:59:55.008 --> 01:00:01.556
This is the last week of our 24th summer
here at Camp Aweegaway.

728
01:00:03.975 --> 01:00:07.353
As my wife used to say,
God is up to something.

729
01:00:08.396 --> 01:00:10.607
He's up to something good.

730
01:00:11.816 --> 01:00:14.277
He's up to something amazing.

731
01:00:16.112 --> 01:00:17.947
That much I know.

732
01:00:31.336 --> 01:00:35.465
I've repeated this
quite a few times to myself.

733
01:00:35.548 --> 01:00:36.633
And um...

734
01:00:38.926 --> 01:00:42.930
These words just mean a lot to me,
so I thought why not share them.

735
01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:49.812
"For I know the plans that I have
in store for you declares the Lord...

736
01:00:52.065 --> 01:00:53.691
plans to prosper you...

737
01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:56.944
not to harm you...

738
01:00:59.572 --> 01:01:02.784
plans to give you a hope...

739
01:01:04.744 --> 01:01:05.744
and a future."

740
01:01:11.918 --> 01:01:13.294
I don't know much.

741
01:01:16.297 --> 01:01:17.465
But this much I do.

742
01:03:43.986 --> 01:03:48.449
That was really cool
what you said about George, I thought.

743
01:03:49.951 --> 01:03:53.621
I think Presley liked it too
I mean, she loved it.

744
01:03:58.626 --> 01:04:00.086
Hey, um... How are y...

745
01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:03.965
How are you feeling about all that?
Because I know it can be...

746
01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:05.508
overwhelming.

747
01:04:05.591 --> 01:04:06.843
It was amazing.

748
01:04:08.261 --> 01:04:09.261
Really?

749
01:04:09.846 --> 01:04:10.846
I don't know.

750
01:04:13.683 --> 01:04:14.559
It's just...

751
01:04:14.642 --> 01:04:15.935
been so long

752
01:04:17.353 --> 01:04:18.521
since I felt so...

753
01:04:21.774 --> 01:04:22.900
connected.

754
01:04:24.193 --> 01:04:26.070
Like I was part of something bigger.

755
01:04:29.740 --> 01:04:30.950
Do you know what I mean?

756
01:04:33.035 --> 01:04:34.120
Yeah, I really do.

757
01:04:37.707 --> 01:04:39.125
- Avery.
- Will.

758
01:04:39.208 --> 01:04:40.084
- Sorry.
- Go head.

759
01:04:40.167 --> 01:04:44.839
Just, can you wait just like two seconds?
I have something for you.

760
01:04:44.922 --> 01:04:47.884
- Oh yeah, sure.
- But just two seconds, okay?

761
01:04:48.384 --> 01:04:49.384
Sorry.

762
01:04:56.058 --> 01:04:58.728
Come on, just tell her the truth.

763
01:05:01.898 --> 01:05:03.024
I, um...

764
01:05:05.985 --> 01:05:09.780
I just wanted you to have this photo.

765
01:05:09.864 --> 01:05:13.117
You don't have to keep it if it's weird.
I just, um...

766
01:05:15.286 --> 01:05:16.996
I don't know, it's a good picture.

767
01:05:21.334 --> 01:05:22.334
Avery, I...

768
01:05:25.963 --> 01:05:26.963
Yeah?

769
01:05:29.550 --> 01:05:30.550
Thank you.

770
01:05:33.429 --> 01:05:34.764
Yeah, it's no problem.

771
01:05:39.226 --> 01:05:42.521
- So, I'll see you tomorrow.
- Yeah, see you tomorrow.

772
01:05:43.105 --> 01:05:44.398
See you tomorrow.

773
01:05:44.482 --> 01:05:45.482
Yeah.

774
01:05:46.025 --> 01:05:47.025
Okay.

775
01:05:50.488 --> 01:05:51.488
Goodnight.

776
01:06:08.673 --> 01:06:10.466
- Oh, hey, Kristin.
- Hey, Will.

777
01:06:10.549 --> 01:06:13.260
Hey, lover boy. How's Avery?

778
01:06:14.136 --> 01:06:15.136
She gave me this.

779
01:06:17.974 --> 01:06:20.726
Man, I look good in this.
Mind if I steal it?

780
01:06:20.810 --> 01:06:22.311
Yeah, I do.

781
01:06:27.692 --> 01:06:29.402
Oh, Will, this is yours.

782
01:06:29.485 --> 01:06:30.485
Thanks.

783
01:06:31.404 --> 01:06:33.572
Oh, wow, are those your parents?

784
01:06:35.199 --> 01:06:36.199
That's them.

785
01:06:37.159 --> 01:06:38.327
Can I see?

786
01:06:39.495 --> 01:06:40.495
Sure.

787
01:06:44.750 --> 01:06:47.003
- You look just like your dad.
- What?

788
01:06:47.086 --> 01:06:48.254
- Yeah.
- Really?

789
01:06:48.337 --> 01:06:51.298
- You got a lot of peach fuzz though.
- Peach fuzz?

790
01:06:51.966 --> 01:06:54.802
Will, your mother is beautiful.

791
01:06:55.469 --> 01:06:56.469
She really is.

792
01:06:57.179 --> 01:07:00.599
You know, your parents
would be really proud of you.

793
01:07:03.019 --> 01:07:04.645
They'd be glad I was here.

794
01:07:14.905 --> 01:07:19.118
I just thought the moment needed
a heartfelt score, it was so tender.

795
01:07:19.201 --> 01:07:20.201
Nice, George.

796
01:07:20.786 --> 01:07:23.956
You know what would be heartfelt?
If you picked up your drawers.

797
01:07:24.040 --> 01:07:26.917
Mom.
Come on, I just wore them.

798
01:07:27.001 --> 01:07:28.919
Do you expect me
to clean my room at camp?

799
01:07:29.003 --> 01:07:31.839
- Why does it smell so bad?
- Boys only.

800
01:07:31.922 --> 01:07:34.341
That boy stink
that just sticks on you.

801
01:07:34.425 --> 01:07:36.177
They smell like old people.

802
01:07:36.260 --> 01:07:38.822
I can smell your shorts.
How long you been wearing them?

803
01:07:38.846 --> 01:07:39.930
They were pants.

804
01:08:07.124 --> 01:08:08.292
Gotcha.

805
01:08:13.964 --> 01:08:14.964
No way.

806
01:08:20.596 --> 01:08:22.848
All right, campers,

807
01:08:22.932 --> 01:08:24.809
now for a Warrior Games update.

808
01:08:24.892 --> 01:08:27.228
In first place the Azure Apostles.

809
01:08:27.311 --> 01:08:28.646
In second the Angels,

810
01:08:28.729 --> 01:08:31.357
and finally Verdes Maximus
coming in third.

811
01:08:31.440 --> 01:08:34.485
Now, don't despair,
I have it from authority on high

812
01:08:34.568 --> 01:08:38.155
that the talent show tonight
is gonna be a game changer.

813
01:08:38.239 --> 01:08:40.407
So warm up those juggling balls,

814
01:08:40.491 --> 01:08:45.121
polish off those tap shoes,
and let's make some magic!

815
01:08:46.288 --> 01:08:48.958
All right,
my fellow Verdes Maximus monsters,

816
01:08:49.458 --> 01:08:53.254
today is the day and if we all do our jobs.

817
01:08:54.213 --> 01:08:55.756
I think tears will be shed,

818
01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:58.092
jaws will be dropped,

819
01:08:58.175 --> 01:09:00.803
and heartstrings will be tugged.

820
01:09:00.886 --> 01:09:04.723
We didn't come this far to be just okay.

821
01:09:05.391 --> 01:09:07.977
- We must be...
- Epic.

822
01:09:09.854 --> 01:09:11.480
What he said.

823
01:09:12.189 --> 01:09:15.401
Let's give it up for our fearless leader
who put this nonsense together, huh?

824
01:09:15.484 --> 01:09:19.655
Okay, we're a team. But, yes,
as the leader I appreciate the validation.

825
01:09:19.738 --> 01:09:21.073
Let's get started.

826
01:09:22.658 --> 01:09:24.493
I am excited.

827
01:09:26.579 --> 01:09:29.456
It'll be nice to have
some decent talent show competition.

828
01:09:29.540 --> 01:09:32.376
- Yeah, this is a closed rehearsal, Sean.
- I'm aware.

829
01:09:32.918 --> 01:09:36.422
I heard the new kid would be playing
a big part in this year's performance.

830
01:09:36.505 --> 01:09:39.216
So I wanted to stop by
and offer a few pointers.

831
01:09:39.758 --> 01:09:41.260
Will, got a minute?

832
01:09:41.343 --> 01:09:43.387
- No, we have to rehearse.
- It's fine.

833
01:09:45.514 --> 01:09:48.142
Sean, if this is about paintball,
I'm sorry, I just...

834
01:09:48.225 --> 01:09:50.394
Hey, you're good. You're good.

835
01:09:50.477 --> 01:09:52.396
You can't change who you are.
I get it.

836
01:09:54.148 --> 01:09:55.900
What's that supposed to mean?

837
01:09:55.983 --> 01:09:57.818
Like, who you really are.

838
01:09:59.445 --> 01:10:00.445
Will Hawkins.

839
01:10:01.697 --> 01:10:02.697
Vandalism,

840
01:10:03.407 --> 01:10:06.160
disorderly conduct, curfew violations.

841
01:10:07.995 --> 01:10:09.038
Auto theft?

842
01:10:11.248 --> 01:10:12.248
You lied.

843
01:10:14.335 --> 01:10:15.920
You're just a big fraud.

844
01:10:17.630 --> 01:10:19.256
And you need to tell Avery.

845
01:10:21.425 --> 01:10:22.425
Or I'm going to.

846
01:10:26.722 --> 01:10:27.722
Look.

847
01:10:29.016 --> 01:10:30.893
I'm trying to do the right thing.

848
01:10:31.810 --> 01:10:32.810
Yeah.

849
01:10:33.771 --> 01:10:34.771
Sure you are.

850
01:10:42.446 --> 01:10:43.781
Keep up the good work.

851
01:10:48.452 --> 01:10:49.578
Hey.

852
01:10:49.662 --> 01:10:51.956
- Uh, hey. Hi, George.
- Okay.

853
01:10:52.039 --> 01:10:53.457
Have you guys seen Will?

854
01:10:53.540 --> 01:10:55.459
- Why? What's up?
- I don't know.

855
01:10:55.542 --> 01:10:58.796
We were trying to rehearse,
Sean walked in, said something to him

856
01:10:58.879 --> 01:11:00.714
and then Will just walked out.

857
01:11:00.798 --> 01:11:03.425
W-wait, Sean? What did Sean say?

858
01:11:03.509 --> 01:11:04.593
I have no idea.

859
01:11:07.137 --> 01:11:08.806
All right, let's go find out.

860
01:11:08.889 --> 01:11:10.808
Come on.

861
01:11:18.899 --> 01:11:20.484
I don't want to tell you this.

862
01:11:23.028 --> 01:11:24.655
Will isn't who he says he is.

863
01:11:26.240 --> 01:11:28.158
What are you talking about?

864
01:11:28.826 --> 01:11:29.826
Ask his cousin.

865
01:11:33.330 --> 01:11:37.584
Six years, seven schools,
twenty-two homes.

866
01:11:37.668 --> 01:11:39.503
You can't change who you are. I get it.

867
01:11:39.586 --> 01:11:41.880
Your parent s would be proud of you.

868
01:11:41.964 --> 01:11:43.549
Vandalism, disorderly conduct.

869
01:11:43.632 --> 01:11:45.944
I don't know if she'd be into
the whole stealing a cop car.

870
01:11:45.968 --> 01:11:50.306
I just choose to believe.
I mean, that's faith, right?

871
01:11:50.389 --> 01:11:51.974
You're just a big fraud.

872
01:11:54.810 --> 01:11:56.895
I'm sorry, but that's the truth.

873
01:11:57.563 --> 01:12:01.775
He's lying to you.
You've gotta believe me.

874
01:12:09.491 --> 01:12:10.492
You're so brave.

875
01:12:16.290 --> 01:12:19.418
Always have an exit plan.

876
01:12:35.934 --> 01:12:36.934
Will.

877
01:13:01.001 --> 01:13:03.087
- Dad! Hi!
- Hi, sweetie.

878
01:13:03.170 --> 01:13:06.090
- Uh, can I have your keys?
- Where are you going?

879
01:13:07.299 --> 01:13:09.259
Sean, I guess said something to Will.

880
01:13:09.343 --> 01:13:12.096
I don't know what he said.
All I know is I checked his cabin.

881
01:13:12.179 --> 01:13:14.264
All of his things are gone, he's gone.

882
01:13:14.348 --> 01:13:16.350
- Well, I'll go look for him.
- No, no.

883
01:13:17.726 --> 01:13:18.726
I need to go.

884
01:13:19.853 --> 01:13:22.940
I think he was trying to say
something to me the other day

885
01:13:23.023 --> 01:13:26.610
or I don't know, but if I go
I think he'll listen to me.

886
01:13:27.277 --> 01:13:28.987
Please, you have to trust me.

887
01:13:49.425 --> 01:13:50.425
Will.

888
01:13:55.639 --> 01:13:56.639
Will.

889
01:13:57.975 --> 01:14:00.602
Will come on, please, where are you going?

890
01:14:01.603 --> 01:14:02.603
Look, I...

891
01:14:03.230 --> 01:14:05.482
I know everything, okay?

892
01:14:05.566 --> 01:14:09.027
Or at least I know some of it.

893
01:14:09.653 --> 01:14:12.656
None of it matters,
so can you please get in the car?

894
01:14:13.323 --> 01:14:16.160
- We can talk about it.
- There's nothing to talk about.

895
01:14:18.579 --> 01:14:19.830
So do you just run away?

896
01:14:21.707 --> 01:14:25.377
- Is that you? Is that the real Will?
- I don't have anybody, Avery.

897
01:14:26.170 --> 01:14:30.007
I don't have a dad to take care of me
or a little magical garden.

898
01:14:32.551 --> 01:14:34.094
That was not fair.

899
01:14:34.178 --> 01:14:35.971
Yeah, you're right. It's not.

900
01:14:36.722 --> 01:14:39.057
It's not fair that my parents
were ripped from me.

901
01:14:39.141 --> 01:14:42.144
That I didn't get
to tell them just once more...

902
01:14:43.395 --> 01:14:47.274
You don't know anything about me.
So don't pretend you do or that you care.

903
01:14:47.357 --> 01:14:49.401
Why do you think I'm standing here now?

904
01:14:49.485 --> 01:14:51.653
- I don't know, you tell me.
- Because I care.

905
01:14:53.238 --> 01:14:57.034
- Because you are so loved.
- By whom? God?

906
01:14:57.117 --> 01:14:58.035
Yes!

907
01:14:58.118 --> 01:15:01.079
Then where was he? Where was he?

908
01:15:01.788 --> 01:15:04.124
He didn't take me that night, no.
He left me there.

909
01:15:06.001 --> 01:15:08.629
He wasn't there for me that night,
hasn't been there since.

910
01:15:08.712 --> 01:15:10.172
What kind of a God is that?

911
01:15:11.757 --> 01:15:12.757
Tell me.

912
01:15:13.717 --> 01:15:17.012
But you know what?
It's fine. I'm fine. Okay?

913
01:15:18.639 --> 01:15:22.643
You're not gonna believe me right now,
when I say this to you but I need you to...

914
01:15:22.726 --> 01:15:24.436
I don't need you to fix me, Avery.

915
01:15:24.520 --> 01:15:27.898
- I'm not trying to fix you, Will.
- Yeah, right.

916
01:15:28.565 --> 01:15:31.527
Fine, then you look at me right now.

917
01:15:31.610 --> 01:15:34.446
- Tell me none of this meant anything.
- Get out of my way.

918
01:15:34.530 --> 01:15:38.075
I can't. Because you can't look at me
and you can't say it.

919
01:15:38.158 --> 01:15:40.994
- Because you know it's not true.
- It meant nothing to me.

920
01:15:41.787 --> 01:15:42.787
What?

921
01:15:44.581 --> 01:15:45.581
None of it.

922
01:15:47.251 --> 01:15:48.251
Can I go now.

923
01:15:59.805 --> 01:16:00.931
Yeah, you can go now.

924
01:16:03.392 --> 01:16:07.020
By the way, you aren't
as good of a liar as you think you are.

925
01:18:31.665 --> 01:18:34.668
Welcome to the talent show!

926
01:18:45.053 --> 01:18:46.221
Wow!

927
01:18:46.304 --> 01:18:49.349
Kristin, I'm looking at the numbers
and with that performance

928
01:18:49.433 --> 01:18:52.310
the Azure Apostles take a commanding lead.

929
01:18:52.394 --> 01:18:55.021
Ahh! Yes!

930
01:18:55.105 --> 01:18:56.189
We're dead.

931
01:18:56.273 --> 01:18:58.692
You tried your best, okay?
It's gonna be fine.

932
01:18:58.775 --> 01:19:00.569
We're gonna have fun, okay?

933
01:19:00.652 --> 01:19:01.653
I know.

934
01:19:02.571 --> 01:19:04.072
Did you find him?

935
01:19:05.449 --> 01:19:06.449
Yeah.

936
01:19:07.033 --> 01:19:10.746
- Yeah, no, I found him.
- Wait, what's going on? Are you okay?

937
01:19:10.829 --> 01:19:13.540
- She. George, she, um...
- I tried.

938
01:19:15.125 --> 01:19:17.169
I don't think he's coming back.

939
01:19:18.712 --> 01:19:20.630
But it's not over yet!

940
01:19:20.714 --> 01:19:24.384
We have our final performance,
Verdes Maximus!

941
01:19:26.803 --> 01:19:33.018
Yeah, that's my baby George.
And this should be epic!

942
01:19:43.320 --> 01:19:45.447
- Go get 'em.
- Thanks, Mom.

943
01:19:57.209 --> 01:19:58.209
I lied.

944
01:19:58.710 --> 01:19:59.710
What?

945
01:20:04.132 --> 01:20:05.592
It meant everything.

946
01:20:10.388 --> 01:20:11.515
All of it.

947
01:20:13.892 --> 01:20:15.560
Thank for coming after me.

948
01:20:19.356 --> 01:20:21.274
Thank you for coming back.

949
01:20:22.776 --> 01:20:24.861
I'm just... I'm so sorry that...

950
01:20:40.126 --> 01:20:41.336
Your fans await.

951
01:20:43.755 --> 01:20:46.258
- We'll talk after, okay?
- Okay.

952
01:20:47.759 --> 01:20:49.177
- You have to go.
- Okay.

953
01:20:49.261 --> 01:20:50.804
Go!

954
01:23:12.028 --> 01:23:17.283
This has been a week of fierce
competition right up to the very end.

955
01:23:17.367 --> 01:23:20.328
I want to say
that I'm proud of all of you.

956
01:23:20.412 --> 01:23:21.871
But in the end, Kristin,

957
01:23:21.955 --> 01:23:26.543
only one team can reign supreme,
and who is it tonight?

958
01:23:31.172 --> 01:23:33.466
Verdes Maximus!

959
01:23:43.059 --> 01:23:45.061
It's all right. It's all right.

960
01:23:46.354 --> 01:23:48.898
Verde! Verde! Verde!

961
01:23:49.983 --> 01:23:54.320
Good morning, campers.
It's a beautiful sunny day.

962
01:23:54.404 --> 01:23:56.865
Everybody up. Everybody moving.

963
01:23:56.948 --> 01:23:59.534
Time to get this party grooving.

964
01:23:59.617 --> 01:24:01.786
It was a week unlike any other.

965
01:24:01.870 --> 01:24:04.956
Today you take home friendships
that will last a lifetime.

966
01:24:05.040 --> 01:24:08.543
Remember that today is not goodbye,
it's see you later.

967
01:24:08.626 --> 01:24:09.711
Go out in the world,

968
01:24:09.794 --> 01:24:12.881
the great big awesome world
and make some magic.

969
01:24:12.964 --> 01:24:14.674
I want to say congratulations.

970
01:24:15.425 --> 01:24:17.427
You killed it.

971
01:24:17.510 --> 01:24:19.220
Thanks, man. It means a lot.

972
01:24:19.763 --> 01:24:20.763
You deserve it.

973
01:24:22.891 --> 01:24:23.892
You can do this.

974
01:24:24.476 --> 01:24:27.312
- Can I talk to you?
- Yeah, what's up?

975
01:24:31.107 --> 01:24:32.107
Man, I just...

976
01:24:33.443 --> 01:24:34.903
just want to say I'm sorry.

977
01:24:36.780 --> 01:24:39.240
You weren't the only one
trying to impress people.

978
01:24:41.076 --> 01:24:44.287
Dude, don't even worry about it.
We're cool.

979
01:24:48.708 --> 01:24:51.294
Yeah, but next year you're going down.

980
01:24:51.377 --> 01:24:52.837
Ahh, we'll see about that.

981
01:24:57.342 --> 01:25:01.012
- Hey, you.
- Hey, mind if I sit here?

982
01:25:01.096 --> 01:25:02.096
Please.

983
01:25:03.807 --> 01:25:04.807
So...

984
01:25:05.892 --> 01:25:07.894
are you coming back next year or what?

985
01:25:09.062 --> 01:25:10.688
Hmm, well, that depends.

986
01:25:10.772 --> 01:25:12.023
Will you be here?

987
01:25:12.941 --> 01:25:13.941
Yes.

988
01:25:14.984 --> 01:25:16.736
Then chances are pretty good.

989
01:25:18.738 --> 01:25:19.948
Hi.

990
01:25:20.615 --> 01:25:21.615
Hey.

991
01:25:30.250 --> 01:25:31.334
I-I-I, um...

992
01:25:33.211 --> 01:25:34.211
Here.

993
01:25:38.591 --> 01:25:41.678
It's beautiful, George.

994
01:25:41.761 --> 01:25:45.932
Um, yeah, the-there are
365 letters in there for you.

995
01:25:46.015 --> 01:25:47.767
Um, I kinda wrote them last year

996
01:25:47.851 --> 01:25:50.061
but I think thematically they could...

997
01:25:51.437 --> 01:25:53.398
I'm sorry.

998
01:25:53.481 --> 01:25:54.816
It's just, um...

999
01:25:56.234 --> 01:25:58.153
"Life moves pretty fast.

1000
01:25:58.236 --> 01:26:02.115
If you don't stop and look around
once in a while you could miss it!"

1001
01:26:02.198 --> 01:26:03.741
From my favorite movie,

1002
01:26:03.825 --> 01:26:05.743
Ferris Bueller's Day Off.

1003
01:26:05.827 --> 01:26:09.455
Wow, someday I'm gonna marry you
Presley Elizabeth Borsky.

1004
01:26:10.081 --> 01:26:14.419
Not if I marry you first
George Montgomery Tanella.

1005
01:26:18.798 --> 01:26:19.798
Here.

1006
01:26:21.050 --> 01:26:22.050
See ya.

1007
01:26:27.348 --> 01:26:29.225
She gave me her number.

1008
01:26:29.309 --> 01:26:32.020
She gave me her number, I...

1009
01:26:32.854 --> 01:26:37.525
Jeez. Should I, like, emoji her?
Is that a thing?

1010
01:26:43.990 --> 01:26:45.533
So what happens next?

1011
01:26:46.117 --> 01:26:48.494
I don't know.
Figure out my next move.

1012
01:26:49.162 --> 01:26:52.415
- I'm gonna miss you, man.
- I'm gonna miss you too.

1013
